521
00:28:31,180 --> 00:28:32,120
A .K .A.

522
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:33,120
Firefist Ace

523
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:37,040
They're gonna execute.

524
00:28:42,620 --> 00:28:46,297
According to this, a pirate
named Blackbeard defeated Ace.

525
00:28:46,380 --> 00:28:48,377
and gave him up to the world government.

526
00:28:48,460 --> 00:28:51,048
In return, they invited
him to be a warlord.

527
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:56,141
Blackbeard, huh?

528
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:58,380
This sends a strong message.

529
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:01,017
The government has
caught a big fish indeed.

530
00:29:01,100 --> 00:29:01,930
But more than that,

531
00:29:02,013 --> 00:29:05,437
if this show of authority can prove that
they're stronger than Whitebeard himself,

532
00:29:05,520 --> 00:29:06,350
well...

533
00:29:06,433 --> 00:29:07,263
Granny!

534
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:09,860
He's just my brother!

535
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:12,900
Por Castilles, the Fire Fist!

536
00:29:13,080 --> 00:29:14,962
You're talking about my brother!

537
00:29:18,940 --> 00:29:19,770
What?

538
00:29:19,853 --> 00:29:21,500
My word! I never knew!

539
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:24,077
Yeah, and I didn't know
anything about this.

540
00:29:24,160 --> 00:29:25,357
He's gonna be killed?

541
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:27,560
But he can still escape, right?

542
00:29:28,820 --> 00:29:33,800
Well, I'd say that his best chance would
be if Whitebeard takes the bait and wins.

543
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:37,880
Tell me, does it say where
they're gonna execute him?

544
00:29:38,560 --> 00:29:42,897
In the town square of Marineford,
where Navy Headquarters is located.

545
00:29:42,980 --> 00:29:46,000
It says the execution will
take place in one week.

546
00:29:46,180 --> 00:29:47,709
That's six days from today

547
00:29:48,680 --> 00:29:49,677
That's too soon!

548
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:53,057
How long will it take to get
from here back to Sabo Odi?

549
00:29:53,140 --> 00:29:56,377
Even at top speed, it would
take more than a week!

550
00:29:56,460 --> 00:29:57,290
A week!

551
00:29:57,373 --> 00:30:00,177
That means by the time
I meet up with my crew?

552
00:30:00,260 --> 00:30:01,477
It'd be too late.

553
00:30:01,560 --> 00:30:02,777
He's would already be dead.

554
00:30:02,860 --> 00:30:07,277
Yes How long to get to where
Aces well if he's being held at

555
00:30:07,360 --> 00:30:11,007
Impel down that would take I
would say a week on a pirate ship

556
00:30:11,580 --> 00:30:14,300
Perhaps four days on a
Navy ship. Whoa, wait!

557
00:30:14,580 --> 00:30:16,537
Since when are Navy ships that fast?

558
00:30:16,620 --> 00:30:21,032
There's a sea current that's reserved
exclusively for the world government.

559
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:26,900
From Inni's lobby, to Impel Down,
to Navy headquarters and back.

560
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:31,480
Think of it as a giant whirlpool
that connects those three facilities.

561
00:30:31,900 --> 00:30:35,540
When the Gates of Justice are
opened at any of these locales,

562
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:37,297
usually to a Navy vessel?

563
00:30:37,380 --> 00:30:41,517
Then the current from the whirlpool
changes and ships are ushered inside.

564
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:44,200
However, if the gates aren't opened,

565
00:30:44,540 --> 00:30:48,177
the ship would keep following the
natural flow of the whirlpool.

566
00:30:48,260 --> 00:30:49,090
Naturally,

567
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:52,737
most pirate ships would rather skip this
current altogether and go the long way.

568
00:30:52,820 --> 00:30:54,517
Though it's convenient for the Navy.

569
00:30:54,600 --> 00:30:56,380
What should I do then?

570
00:31:00,460 --> 00:31:02,080
What do you want to do?

571
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,460
Don't tell me!

572
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:06,758
You have your brother's beaver card?

573
00:31:08,380 --> 00:31:12,160
Uh, is that the moving paper
that you care so much about?

574
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:14,517
Nuh-uh, that one was a different one.

575
00:31:14,600 --> 00:31:16,620
This is the card that Ace gave me.

576
00:31:18,400 --> 00:31:21,160
They're also known as the paper of life,

577
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:24,397
since they give you a hint about
the person's state of health?

578
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:26,068
as well as their direction.

579
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:28,697
Then, if it's that small, that means...

580
00:31:28,780 --> 00:31:32,192
Back when he first gave it to
me, it was ten times bigger.

581
00:31:35,140 --> 00:31:37,434
Looks like Ace has been busy on his own

582
00:31:37,940 --> 00:31:38,770
adventure.

583
00:31:38,853 --> 00:31:43,860
It's perfectly natural for a guy
to worry about his bungling kid

584
00:31:46,060 --> 00:31:46,890
brother.

585
00:31:46,973 --> 00:31:49,817
Ace wouldn't be happy about
his little brother saving him,

586
00:31:49,900 --> 00:31:52,194
but that's still better than him dying.

587
00:31:55,800 --> 00:32:00,117
Either way, I'm gonna need
to take a little side trip.

588
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:01,400
Sorry everyone.

589
00:32:07,200 --> 00:32:08,357
I have to save him.

590
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:10,264
He's the only brother I've got.

591
00:32:12,060 --> 00:32:14,295
Perhaps you should think this through.

592
00:32:14,380 --> 00:32:17,660
Do you have any idea how
reckless this plan is?

593
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,940
You're facing a full-fledged war.

594
00:32:20,580 --> 00:32:24,109
You'll be nothing more than a
leaf whipped about by a storm,

595
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:27,960
an insect flicked away by hands
far mightier than your own.

596
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:29,997
Yeah, that doesn't matter to me.

597
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:31,340
I still gotta try.

598
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:34,437
I couldn't live with myself
if I let this happen.

599
00:32:34,520 --> 00:32:35,755
I gotta do something.

600
00:32:37,520 --> 00:32:38,940
Yes, I can see that.

601
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:44,940
So then, you plan to rescue the
most infamous prisoner in the world.

602
00:32:45,660 --> 00:32:48,540
I give you a one in a
million chance of success.

603
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:53,661
But in order to even try, you need to get
to the great prison where he's being held.

604
00:32:56,300 --> 00:32:58,620
Once they transport him to Marineford,

605
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:03,586
both the admirals and the warlords will
be keeping a close eye on the situation.

606
00:33:04,200 --> 00:33:05,030
Keep in mind,

607
00:33:05,280 --> 00:33:09,477
because your brother is the most
important prisoner in the Navy's custody,

608
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:11,517
the prison will be carefully guarded,

609
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:15,077
and it has quite the fearsome
reputation if you haven't heard.

610
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:18,280
It may prove impossible
to enter no matter what.

611
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:20,517
I'll worry about that when I get there.

612
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:21,776
There's no time now.

613
00:33:21,920 --> 00:33:24,617
I gotta make it before they
take Ace to be executed.

614
00:33:24,700 --> 00:33:27,817
Give me the biggest door you've
got, and I'll paddle like hell.

615
00:33:27,900 --> 00:33:29,220
Now hold on a second.

616
00:33:29,460 --> 00:33:32,077
You'll never reach the prison
by determination alone.

617
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:34,740
There is a slim chance this could work,

618
00:33:34,900 --> 00:33:38,517
but the snake princess is
refusing to follow the order for

619
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:41,894
the seven warlords to assemble
But what if that changed?

620
00:33:42,080 --> 00:33:43,600
If she obeyed that order,

621
00:33:43,940 --> 00:33:48,457
we could take advantage of the situation
and sneak you on board their ship Wait,

622
00:33:48,540 --> 00:33:49,370
what are you?

623
00:33:49,453 --> 00:33:51,200
You mean there's a navy ship here?

624
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:54,382
Great, then I'm gonna go
ask her if she'll do it?

625
00:34:01,040 --> 00:34:02,197
Greninion, it's terrible!

626
00:34:02,280 --> 00:34:04,860
Inishida, what's all the fuss about?

627
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:09,774
Thank goodness I found you quickly
when I heard I came as fast as I could

628
00:34:10,340 --> 00:34:11,200
Heard what?

629
00:34:11,940 --> 00:34:13,040
It's awful.

630
00:34:15,500 --> 00:34:16,820
The snake princess.

631
00:34:18,020 --> 00:34:19,577
She's come down with a sickness.

632
00:34:19,660 --> 00:34:22,140
And no one knows what it is?

633
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:24,350
Ah!

634
00:34:24,433 --> 00:34:26,140
She's sick! Oh, no!

635
00:34:31,720 --> 00:34:33,600
Whatever it is, fight it!

636
00:34:34,500 --> 00:34:35,330
Don't give up.

637
00:34:35,413 --> 00:34:36,700
Please stay strong.

638
00:34:37,960 --> 00:34:40,842
What's this about the
snake princess falling ill?

639
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:42,940
Oh, Couran and Yon.

640
00:34:47,620 --> 00:34:49,700
Man, I need you to wait outside.

641
00:34:50,220 --> 00:34:51,417
What? But why?

642
00:34:51,500 --> 00:34:53,440
I'm in a hurry! I knew that!

643
00:34:59,520 --> 00:35:00,520
It hurts.

644
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:04,200
She keeps clutching her chest.

645
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:07,031
Perhaps something is wrong with her heart.

646
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:13,421
I've never seen anything like it.

647
00:35:14,820 --> 00:35:16,537
Since her symptoms are a mystery,

648
00:35:16,620 --> 00:35:19,337
there's very little I can
do in terms of treatment.

649
00:35:19,420 --> 00:35:21,949
All we know is that
it's extremely painful.

650
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:25,315
She won't eat a thing and
she's hardly speaking either.

651
00:35:31,980 --> 00:35:33,020
Tomorrow morning.

652
00:35:33,560 --> 00:35:34,760
What are you doing?

653
00:35:35,020 --> 00:35:38,020
Whatever it is, Granny
Nyon, you've got to stop it.

654
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:41,240
Yes, of course. That fool.

655
00:35:41,520 --> 00:35:42,920
I should have realized.

656
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:48,360
It's a pity that the virus came
at a time like this. Huh? Virus?

657
00:35:48,680 --> 00:35:51,037
If you know what it is, then just tell us.

658
00:35:51,120 --> 00:35:53,420
I can't breathe, Granny Magellan.

659
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:57,900
Am I going to die like this?

660
00:35:58,980 --> 00:36:00,540
Indeed, yes.

661
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:02,235
I'll say it isn't so.

662
00:36:02,380 --> 00:36:05,357
If this is supposed to be
a joke, we're not laughing.

663
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:07,200
It has killed us before.

664
00:36:07,760 --> 00:36:10,160
It took the life of our last Empress.

665
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:15,497
The same fate befell the
Empress before her, too.

666
00:36:15,580 --> 00:36:20,286
I suffered from the illness myself, but
left the country before it took my life.

667
00:36:20,420 --> 00:36:22,200
No remedy could save me

668
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:24,660
Snake princess monkey D.

669
00:36:24,760 --> 00:36:26,677
Luffy has come to see you as well.

670
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:30,340
This is hardly the time He
has a request to ask of you.

671
00:36:30,520 --> 00:36:31,860
Will you hear it?

672
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:33,511
What do you mean request?

673
00:36:33,640 --> 00:36:35,017
Can't you see she's suffering?

674
00:36:35,100 --> 00:36:36,629
How important could it be?

675
00:36:37,700 --> 00:36:41,700
What just happened show him in quickly

676
00:36:48,980 --> 00:36:50,020
Monkey D.

677
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:53,720
Luffy, you are a man favored by fate.

678
00:36:54,100 --> 00:36:56,747
Perhaps this mountain
can be moved after all.

679
00:36:56,960 --> 00:36:59,660
And perhaps you are the one to do it.

680
00:37:00,900 --> 00:37:02,520
I hear you need something.

681
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:06,000
Yeah, I sure do.

682
00:37:06,360 --> 00:37:07,517
But are you okay?

683
00:37:07,600 --> 00:37:08,894
I heard you were sick.

684
00:37:09,020 --> 00:37:09,961
Never mind that.

685
00:37:10,100 --> 00:37:11,740
No illness can overtake me.

686
00:37:12,080 --> 00:37:14,317
There's a pirate on
Whitebeard's crew named Ace.

687
00:37:14,400 --> 00:37:16,977
He's my brother, and he's
about to be executed.

688
00:37:17,060 --> 00:37:18,540
I gotta go rescue him.

689
00:37:19,020 --> 00:37:21,877
But I heard if we took a
pirate ship, it'd be too slow.

690
00:37:21,960 --> 00:37:24,197
So instead of going back to my friends,

691
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:27,456
I need you to get on a Navy
ship and take me with you.

692
00:37:27,760 --> 00:37:31,040
How dare you even suggest
that, you selfish beast?

693
00:37:31,380 --> 00:37:33,897
You know full well the
horrors our poor sister went

694
00:37:33,980 --> 00:37:37,333
through and steal you a dragger
to that abhorrent prison?

695
00:37:38,500 --> 00:37:40,100
How can you be so cruel?

696
00:37:40,220 --> 00:37:42,037
This is exactly why we hate men.

697
00:37:42,120 --> 00:37:45,237
We very well could have killed you,
but as soon as we show you mercy,

698
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:46,677
then you let it go to your head.

699
00:37:46,760 --> 00:37:49,157
You're lucky she doesn't turn
you to stone and smash you.

700
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:53,769
You want me to follow the government's
orders and go with the other warlords?

701
00:37:55,240 --> 00:37:56,240
He's said enough.

702
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:57,620
Strike him down.

703
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:05,320
If that is truly your request, then of
course, I will go anywhere you like.

704
00:38:08,980 --> 00:38:11,060
Whoa, thanks. I was worried.

705
00:38:11,300 --> 00:38:13,617
I don't know what I would
have done without your help.

706
00:38:13,700 --> 00:38:15,340
She actually said yes.

707
00:38:15,580 --> 00:38:18,477
She wouldn't listen to reason,
but she'll listen to him.

708
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:20,266
What happened to her, Granny?

709
00:38:20,620 --> 00:38:22,217
Like the Empress before her,

710
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:27,360
our Empress succumbed to the burning
flames that are known only as love.

711
00:38:30,180 --> 00:38:33,617
There's a saying in the East Blue
that describes these winds of passion.

712
00:38:33,700 --> 00:38:35,417
Love is...

713
00:38:35,500 --> 00:38:37,497
Always... A...

714
00:38:37,580 --> 00:38:38,920
Moving on!
